"""agent-history — one history for all your AI coding agents.

Browse, search and resume the conversations you've had with your coding agents,
across all your projects, in one terminal app.

Supported agents: @AGENTS@

Usage:
  agent-history [query]          open the app, optionally with an initial search
  agent-history --agent NAME [query]
                                 show only one agent's conversations (@NAMES@)
  agent-history --list           print a plain list (date, agent, project, title)
  agent-history --help           show this help
  agent-history --version        show the version

Agents can be switched on/off in the app (key: s) or in the config file
~/.config/agent-history/config.toml (AGENT_HISTORY_CONFIG overrides the path):
  [agents]
  @EXAMPLE@
Agents missing from the file are on. --agent NAME shows that agent for the run
even if it's switched off.

Environment:
  AGENT_HISTORY_LANG    "en" or "it" (default: from LANG / LC_ALL)
  AGENT_HISTORY_CONFIG  config file path
  AGENT_HISTORY_ROOTS   colon-separated folder names under $HOME that hold your
                        repos (default: Dev:dev:code:src:projects:repos:git:workspace:Developer)
  Each agent's own data-dir variable is honoured too: CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR (Claude Code),
  CODEX_HOME (Codex), PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR / PI_CODING_AGENT_SESSION_DIR (pi).

https://github.com/formich/agent-history — MIT License
"""
